    {
      "sceneId": "rearranging-a-booking",
      "kind": "stories",
      "itemId": "rearranging-a-booking",
      "src": "/audio/stories/rearranging-a-booking.mp3",
      "text": "Owen calls a pottery studio to move a booking for two people from Saturday to Sunday. “Could we move our session to the afternoon?” he asks. The receptionist says the afternoon is full, but two places are available at ten in the morning. “If there is no extra charge, we could take the morning session,” Owen replies. “The price stays the same, but any change depends on availability when you call back before five today,” she explains. “Could you keep the original booking until then?” he asks, because his friend has not agreed yet. She agrees to keep Saturday booked but warns that the Sunday places cannot be held without confirmation. Owen will check with his friend and call back before five, knowing that Sunday may no longer be available.",
      "textSha256": "22cd8296859356329b33761dad88019eb981f58d1400cad32b297aada4e657d5",
      "voiceId": "kokoro-af-heart-v1",
      "sha256": "e8d239048119a2ce112b1c270e8e5679cbdb3c5745f9d5895e96cf07517018b6",
      "duration": 44.025,
      "graphemes": [
        "Owen calls a pottery studio to move a booking for two people from Saturday to Sunday. “Could we move our session to the afternoon?” he asks. The receptionist says the afternoon is full, but two places are available at ten in the morning. “If there is no extra charge, we could take the morning session,” Owen replies. “The price stays the same, but any change depends on availability when you call back before five today,” she explains. “Could you keep the original booking until then?”",
        "he asks, because his friend has not agreed yet. She agrees to keep Saturday booked but warns that the Sunday places cannot be held without confirmation. Owen will check with his friend and call back before five, knowing that Sunday may no longer be available."
      ],
